# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and edit the copy. Never put passwords or tokens in it: it is not a secret store.

# --- Hosting: Docker Compose and `npm run serve` ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The address of your Jellyfin server as your BROWSER reaches it: the IP address or the domain name of the machine that
# runs Jellyfin, with its port. Never "localhost": that would mean the device you are browsing from, not your server.
# Optional. It only pre-fills the sign-in screen, and each person can still type another address.
JELLYFIN_URL=
# The port Jellyflix is served on.
JELLYFLIX_PORT=8080
# Optional: the extra modules container (see ../modules/README.md). Leave both empty and the app never looks for one.
#   JELLYFLIX_MODULES_URL         where THIS container reaches it, e.g. http://jellyflix-modules:8097 (nginx passes /modules/ on to it)
#   JELLYFLIX_MODULES_PUBLIC_URL  or: the address your BROWSER uses for it, e.g. http://192.168.1.50:8097 (no proxy)
# With `npm run serve` only JELLYFLIX_MODULES_URL is read, and it must be the address your BROWSER uses.
JELLYFLIX_MODULES_URL=
JELLYFLIX_MODULES_PUBLIC_URL=

# --- Development only (`npm run dev`) ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same idea, baked into the development build. Put it in ".env.local" if you would rather not keep it in this file.
# VITE_DEFAULT_SERVER_URL=http://YOUR-JELLYFIN-IP:8096
